Jumbo Frame is a frame that is maximum 9,000 bytes.

Normal Frame is 9000 bytes

These frames contain 2 things: 

- Frame Payload
- Frame Overhead

These are shared across the physical medium.

Normal Frames:

With normal frames you have more overhead to payload ration. More wasted time on medium.

More Frames = More space between frames 

More wasted time on medium

Jumbo Frames:

More payload (data) per frame overhead = more efficiency

More payload per frame = less frames = less wastes between frame

Drawbacks:

Every step has to support jumbo Frames or you will see fragmentation BAD.

Not everything in AWS support jumbo frames

Do and Don’t for Jumbo Frames:

Do: 

- Same region peering
- Direct Connect
- Traffic over an internet gateway

Don’t: 

- Traffic outside a single VPC
- Traffic over an inter-region VPC peering connection
- Traffic over VPN connections
- Traffic over an internet gateway
